cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, cite the repository revision (commit hash) and
  the specific theorem note, for example notes/2026-09-30-six-generation.md
  for Theorem G. A DOI will be added here once a release is archived.
type: software
title: >-
  Six-point homometry in finite cyclic groups: a computer-assisted generating
  theorem with certificates
authors:
  - family-names: Bown
    given-names: Hunter
    email: hmbown@gmail.com
version: 2026.10.04
date-released: 2026-10-04
repository-code: https://github.com/Hmbown/six-point-homometry
keywords:
  - homometric sets
  - Z-relation
  - interval content
  - phase retrieval
  - cyclic groups
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  For every positive integer n, the translation/reflection classes of
  six-element subsets of Z/nZ with equal pairwise-distance multisets are
  exactly the connected components of an explicit construction graph
  (Theorem G). The repository contains the written proofs, separate
  adversarial reviews, exact computational certificates, an independent
  proof-checker replay of the six-atom line theorem's certificates, Lean 4 proofs of the
  elementary soundness lemmas, and an exact count of the classical Bloom
  construction's pair edges for every modulus. The research, code and
  reviews were produced with substantial AI assistance under the author's
  direction; the work has not been externally peer reviewed.
